@@ -507,7 +507,7 @@
     URLs and titles of pages you visit are sent to Google Cloud or third parties for analysis, and may be visible to your administrator. For example, they might be scanned to detect unsafe websites or filter websites based on rules set by the administrator.
   </message>
   <message name="IDS_MANAGEMENT_ENTERPRISE_REPORTING_VISIBLE_DATA" desc="Description of the visible data for the Connectors reporting feature" formatter_data="android_java">
-    When security events are flagged by Chrome, relevant data about the events is sent to your administrator. This can include URLs and titles of pages you visit in Chrome, URLs of pages you copied data from, file names or metadata, IP addresses, browser or tab crashes, and the username that you use to sign in to web based applications, your device and Chrome.
+    When security events are flagged by Redrob, relevant data about the events is sent to your administrator. This can include URLs and titles of pages you visit in Redrob, URLs of pages you copied data from, file names or metadata, IP addresses, browser or tab crashes, and the username that you use to sign in to web based applications, your device and Redrob.
   </message>
 
